import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 661 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 662 | 2026-10-26 | **Chapter 6, Listen and Sing: the Beginner floor's aural room (decided 25 Oct; the decision board's build queue, item 1; her 01:13 'fill the balance as you see it').** Built on row 661. Ears first, on the keys only, in C position; rhythms in chapter 3's beat words (walk, run-ning). Its Lesson Book (lsLbPages, 7 pages) is its online lesson: opener ('Ears first. Listen, sing it back, then find it on the keys.'); Step 1 Keep the beat (LsBeatPad: a tune over C and G chords, tap every beat, the music stops for bar 3, the beat does not; scored on the audio clock with plMatch); Step 2 Echo the rhythm (LsEchoPad: two bars heard, two bars tapped straight back, a soft click keeping the pulse; six rhythms of walk, run-ning, holds and one silent beat); Step 3 Up or down (LsUpDownPad: two notes, up towards the bird, down towards the turtle, or the same; the keys show 1 and 2 after); Step 4 Find your note (LsFindPad: hear a note C-G, sing it on 'la', find it in C position, 'higher: towards the bird' / 'lower: towards the turtle'); Step 5 Sing it back (LsSingPad: three notes, then five, sing then play, right hand C position); My five checks. Teacher notes on every page (sing at a comfortable pitch; the app cannot hear singing: the teacher's ear decides). Drill, six heard levels, no paper (LISTEN_DRILL noPrint): up or down, low/middle/high (turtle, Clara, bird), same or different rhythm, same or different tune, which shape (up-up, down-down, up-down, down-up), find the note. Home: a seventh door, Aural (between Pieces and Stories of music): 'Listen and sing' (the chapter's five lessons, ls-beat ... ls-sing, made from the book's pages with lbhSpec, its questions heard; check: the chapter) and 'More listening' (hear-find, echo, touch-ear, ch-ear, iv-mh, iv-ear, csx-ear). The house: room 6, its chip Aural / 청음. Chapters 6 onward renumber (Notes & rests 7, Loud & soft 8, The staff 9 ...); every chapter reference in the books is bkChapterNo, so it follows. Also: chapter 5's contents list is now Korean on the Korean page. Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch686.py, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/lsx.jsx, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/lsh.jsx. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
